    "result_text": "The build is green. The full test suite (2 tests) passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented rejection of owner creation when the normalized telephone is already used by another owner, returning HTTP 409.\n\nChanges made (following standard Spring layering \u2014 controller \u2192 service \u2192 repository):\n\n1. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 after normalizing the telephone to 10 digits, it now checks whether any existing owner already has that telephone and returns `409 CONFLICT` if so, before saving.\n\n2. **`ClinicService` / `ClinicServiceImpl`** \u2014 added `findOwnerByTelephone(String telephone)` (read-only transactional) delegating to the repository.\n\n3. **`OwnerRepository`** \u2014 added `findByTelephone(String telephone)` to the interface, implemented across all three profiles:\n   - **Spring Data JPA** (`SpringDataOwnerRepository`, the active profile) \u2014 `@Query` deriving owners by telephone.\n   - **JPA** (`JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl`) \u2014 JPQL query.\n   - **JDBC** (`JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl`) \u2014 parameterized SQL query.\n\nThe check uses the normalized telephone (digits-only, exactly 10), so comparison is against the same canonical form that gets persisted. Both new acceptance tests (`coreRejectsDuplicateTelephone`, `functionalityAllowsDistinctTelephone`) pass, and the full suite builds green.",
